  "fhs": {
    "inputContract": "The existing ten-key quantum_geometry_lab input is unchanged. fhsReplay is the only additional public result key; SSH has null.",
    "dataOrigin": "Four raw forward overlaps and endpoint phases from the same existing eigensolver and _fhs arrays, in two fixed base-grid cells.",
    "gridOwnership": "Replay mesh N matches convergence[0] and heatmap. The existing main topology value belongs to the fine 2N-1 grid; two cells do not replace the full Brillouin-zone sum.",
    "validity": "Global isolated-band status and normalized-link validity are separate. Closed-gap loop/flux remain null; raw finite-grid contractions are diagnostic only. Fixed periodic orbital basis uses identity sewing.",
    "display": "The four oriented factors include two conjugates; multiply complex factors before minus-Arg. Edge principal phases, their sum and the dimensionless branch integer are shown with separate units."
  },
  "operatorActions": "Declared axial-spin transformations and endpoint transposition distinguish one inversion from combined constraints. Closed-system Pauli commutators are added elementwise before norms; a finite active pi rotation is distinguished from a continuous generator and a passive basis change.",
  "chiralityActions": "Proper same-label mirror registration and per-atom residuals are distinguished from structure self-symmetries. Generator fixed-vector equations select allowed polar subspaces; zero response remains symmetry-allowed.",
