  "verification": [
    "Independent analytic frames and explicit loops check orientation, boundaries, U(1) covariance, branch choices and invalid overlaps; the production eigensolver is not repeated to manufacture replay data.",
    "The actual current result is used after explicit result-panel expansion; old records or SSH show scope guidance. Finite learning references are separately identified and copied only through existing supported schemas.",
    "Native disclosures, unfinished predictions and notes, original incomplete forms, ordinary tab changes, DOM ownership, stale asynchronous loaders/copy and manual-Run transitions are exercised in actual binders with non-Array NodeList semantics.",
    "Source hashes use UTF-8/LF. Numerical captures use declared tight tolerances and subspace/projector checks rather than arbitrary SVD signs; computation inputs and result identity are preserved."
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "The two-cell FHS trace is an operational teaching view of the declared two-band periodic-orbital model, not a general Bloch-sewing or real-material Chern classifier.",
    "Finite spin references do not replace the existing full tensor/commutator tools, treat a single initial trajectory as an operator proof, or infer SU(2) from total S squared.",
    "Mirror-fit minimizers and SVD bases need not be unique. Allowed polar directions do not provide material response magnitudes or establish ferroelectric switching.",
    "The 197-lesson depth review, targeted diagnosis and authentic scientific-workflow coverage remain incomplete. The production optional graph connects all 197 inventory lessons through 259 edges; this does not establish complete operational depth. No student learning gains are inferred."
